ps://www.discogs.com/artist/13332006-DJ-Sinceer","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/158787/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"158787","image":"https://i.discogs.com/EzzsdmGJPnJaUlWwIZWXGC7aMBBgmGLDA2FMOdDMQzA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1ODc4/Ny0xNjA0MzUxNjY3/LTkzMzIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/L69ZFg81bOU4OpsZPIeAnptbzp1MLGWq8U5dUTPoego/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1ODc4/Ny0xNjA0MzUxNjY3/LTkzMzIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Jamaican DJ Super Cat, born in 1966 in Seivright Gardens, Kingston, started his career as a soundsystem live-DJ in the 1970s, toasting under the alias of Cat-A-Rock. In 1982, his first single, \"Mr. Walker\", was released for [a=Winston Riley]'s Techniques label. After a short term in jail, he used to be regular DJ on [a=Killamanjaro] sound, where he got the nickname \"Wild Apache\". With his spree of hits in the 2nd half of the 1980s he became one of the most popular DJs of Jamaica. In the beginning of the 1990s Super Cat moved to New York and signed a major deal with Columbia; several albums and singles followed. In the second half of the 1990s Super Cat seemingly sunk into oblivion; the attempt to start a comeback through the Neptunes' [l=Star Trak Entertainment] label did not work out. Yet, Super Cat remains one of the most legendary DJs in dancehall history. Due to this fact, as well as due to his over-restrictive dubplate cutting policy, Super Cat dubplates are a 100% killer tool in a soundclash if you are one of the very few lucky soundmen to own one. Super Cat was a major influence for many DJs to come - the most known examples are [a=Shaggy] and  [a=Sean Paul]. In fact, many young and less musically educated listeners have been observed to mistake Super Cat recordings for unknown Sean Paul tunes.\r\nOlder brother of [a=Junior Cat].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:158787","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":232950,"name":"William Maragh"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Mr. Cat","S. Cat","S.Cat","Supa Cat","Supacat","Supakat","Super \"Wild Apache\" Cat","Super - Cat","Super Cat (The Indian)","Super Man","Super-Cat","SuperCat","Superact","Supercat","Supercate"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/158787-Super-Cat-2","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/194282/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"194282","image":"https://i.discogs.com/gtcuzTNr-T3paq9eX6bXR58zsb2VvDGmdvJhHLxMwgU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:405/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5NDI4/Mi0xNTk0NTE3MjI2/LTczMTYuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/KoLtz-XOPzWcJ-GXizlPgwmILagxdZcYh_hqVIOO9Uk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5NDI4/Mi0xNTk0NTE3MjI2/LTczMTYuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"DJ Screw (born July 20, 1971, Smithville, Texas, USA – died November 16, 2000, Houston, Texas, USA) was an American hip hop DJ who was based in Houston, Texas. DJ Screw originated the \"Chopped & Screwed\" style of chopping records and slowing down the recorded mix afterwards. DJ Screw made his name by releasing hundreds of screwed mix tapes, which consisted of songs and freestyle sessions. Screw would sometimes but rarely freestyle on a few of his tapes, including songs like the \"Riding High\" Freestyle & \"I Got 5\" Freestyle.\r\nScrew was the centerpiece of The Screwed Up Click, the rap collective from Houston. An interesting observation should be made - contrary to the trend of releasing entire albums from one artist Screwed & Chopped.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:194282","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":3620427,"name":"Robert Earl Davis, Jr."}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["D, Screw","D.J. Screw","D.J.Screw","DJ Scew","DJ Screw It","DJ. Screw","Dj Csrew","Screw","Screw On Tables","Scrwe","The Late D.J Screw"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/194282-DJ-